{"skill":{"slug":"github","displayName":"Github"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545344344,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1113,"sha256":"51b28818a6f0359287d5c8244a6fdc59a4ac5504596deb193b28b81832221c86","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1449,"sha256":"9f6111874f7cbaa3661e90c129b94d546242ea5520decbb75d60a5fec7e52ef8","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013562132,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d0bef7d74621458724b7de544cdcedd8aaee25f00bb43142a85bc9ce62b0c2d7","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d0bef7d74621458724b7de544cdcedd8aaee25f00bb43142a85bc9ce62b0c2d7","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: github\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides instructions for interacting with GitHub using the `gh` CLI. All examples provided in `SKILL.md` demonstrate read-only operations (e.g., checking PR status, listing runs, viewing API data). While the `gh api` command itself offers broad capabilities that could be misused if the agent's GitHub token has extensive permissions, the skill's instructions and examples do not show any intent for malicious behavior, data exfiltration, prompt injection, or other high-risk actions. The content is clearly aligned with its stated purpose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159612649},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789013562132},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill gives normal GitHub CLI usage guidance and does not show hidden, persistent, or unrelated behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Using gh can rely on the user's local GitHub authentication and network access, which is expected for a GitHub integration but should be used with user-confirmed repo and command scope.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact is a Markdown skill file only, with no executable installer, dependency setup, or package-install instructions.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Instructions are concise and task-scoped, including repo selection guidance; the gh api escape hatch is disclosed as an advanced query mechanism rather than hidden behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No persistence, background workers, memory writes, privilege escalation, credential harvesting, or tool wrapping behavior appears in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to interact with GitHub using the gh CLI, and the artifact provides examples for PR checks, workflow runs, failed logs, API queries, and JSON filtering that fit that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, understand that this skill may guide an agent to use your authenticated gh CLI session. That is appropriate for GitHub work, but review commands that mutate issues, PRs, workflows, or repository settings before allowing them to run.","findings":null,"agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013562132}}}}}